# Command replacement candidates, shared by Bash and Zsh.
#
# Three fields separated by `|`: the command name, the candidates to try on
# macOS, and the candidates to try on Linux. Within a field, candidates are
# separated by spaces and ordered from most preferred to last; the first one
# that is installed wins, and a command with no installed candidate keeps the
# platform default by being left unaliased.
#
# The two platform columns are deliberately different rather than merged.
# macOS goes modern replacement -> GNU tool -> platform default, because the
# platform default is BSD; Linux goes modern replacement -> default command
# with no `g`-prefixed detour, because the default is already GNU. Merging the
# columns would make `gls` and `gsed` candidates on Linux too, which is not
# what this configuration wants even where no such executable exists.
#
# Add a command row or insert a compatible replacement into a column. Do not
# list tools whose command-line interface differs from the command they would
# replace. Implementation-specific flags belong in the consumers' presets
# (notably eza versus ls), not here.
#
# Consumed by apps/zsh/core/aliases.zsh and apps/bash/aliases.bash. Neither
# forks to read it.

# command | macos                | linux
ls        | eza gls ls           | eza ls
tree      | eza tree             | eza tree
vim       | nvim vim             | nvim vim
vi        | nvim vi              | nvim vi
sed       | gsed sed             | sed
grep      | ggrep grep           | grep
find      | gfind find           | find
xargs     | gxargs xargs         | xargs
tar       | gtar tar             | tar
dircolors | gdircolors dircolors | dircolors
git       | git                  | git
ports     | lsof                 | ss netstat
